  ESTIMATOR PRECISION = 2x the T-law scatter (M ~ T^2): X-COP 0.103 dex, HeCS 0.356 dex, E11 0.166 dex; the 0.062-dex T benchmark -> 0.124-dex mass precision
  PLACE AMONG THE ESTIMATORS (relative registers): weak lensing M500 calibration uncertainty on the committed eRASS1 columns = 0.075 fractional (0.031 dex); the SZ/YX mass proxies and X-ray T-M scaling sit at the 0.1-0.15-dex scatter class (literature-level registers, not re-sourced here); the framework thermometer's within-sample precision 0.10-0.36 dex (0.10-0.17 on the homogeneous X-COP/E11 legs) is the SZ-class, with ZERO free parameters (no fitted M-T slope, no calibration to the data).

