============================================================================================
PART 3 -- THE SYSTEMATICS: the honest error budget
============================================================================================
  mu ASSUMPTION (baseline 0.6): T_pred scales ~ mu; delta log10 r = log10(mu/0.6): mu = 0.55 -> -0.038 dex, mu = 0.61 -> +0.007, mu = 0.63 -> +0.021, mu = 0.65 -> +0.035 dex on the amplitude (2x on M_impl); a plausible fully-ionized [0.59, 0.62] band moves the median by [-0.007, +0.014] dex -- below the 0.05-dex scatter
  HSE BIAS: G095-registered HSE scatter 0.053 dex on the X-COP M500/T system; the eRASS1 core-KT-vs-kTvir cross-instrument offset MEASURED here on the 5 X-COP overlaps: mean -0.109, rms 0.138 dex (eRASS1 cooler) -- the HeCS leg's dominant T systematic
  f_b FLOOR: the +0.02 star fraction (of M500) vs the eRASS1-loader 1.2xM_gas prescription over the 38 E11+HeCS objects: median delta on log10 T_pred = -0.0143 dex (M_b moves by +/-a few %, T by half of that) -- a sub-0.01-dex term, below the scatter; the cosmic-f_b floor question is S05's register, carried
  THE AMPLITUDE GAP (registered and carried): identity-form medians 0.43-0.72 (/2 floors 0.22-0.36) vs the observed medians; the X-COP leg reproduces G075's registered 0.280 (canonical 0.28007) at the horizon footing; the total-mass virial floor explanation f = M_dyn/M_b = 5.664 (G095 median), closed form 2 f (r_M/r) = 3.512 vs T_obs/T_floor = 3.572: the observed T is the virial temperature of the TOTAL mass -- the baryon-floor gap is geometry + content (f), not a scaling failure; NOT re-fit here, carried into V3

